# UBSan suppressions. Only third-party code (MTA's vendored Lua 5.1), never the module.
#
# Lua 5.1 luaH_getnum: `cast(unsigned int, key-1)` overflows for key == INT_MIN, which happens
# when a script uses a huge number as a table key (luaH_get's lua_number2int saturates on
# x86). Upstream Lua 5.1 behaviour, triggered by the scenario's own table constructors
# ({[2^40] = 1}); unrelated to ml_pgsql.
signed-integer-overflow:luaH_getnum
